      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, agreed. I replaced the two-byte memcpy helpers with explicit byte loads and stores that assemble and disassemble each UV pair.\n\nThe original casts are undefined in C++ when the UV buffer is not naturally aligned, even though common x86 and Arm CPUs support unaligned halfword accesses in hardware.\n\nI kept the RVV dispatch checks because those kernels pass typed `uint16_t*`/`uint32_t*` pointers to e16/e32 memory intrinsics. The `SSE` and `NEON` assembly paths already support unaligned loads and stores.",
